1
00:00:02,287 --> 00:00:05,220
Wow! You guys act like
you’re never coming back!

2
00:00:07,928 --> 00:00:10,548
I mean, make sure to come home often, okay?

3
00:00:11,078 --> 00:00:12,018
Of course!

4
00:00:12,043 --> 00:00:15,977
We just need to finish our contract,
or else the company might sue us.

5
00:00:16,727 --> 00:00:18,740
Oh well, just keep
bussing in Singapore, okay?

6
00:00:18,851 --> 00:00:20,025
Hey, give me a "slay"!

7
00:00:20,184 --> 00:00:22,078
Slay!

8
00:00:24,689 --> 00:00:27,023
Oh, my grandkids...

9
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:27,906
Lola...

10
00:00:28,017 --> 00:00:31,344
So, you’re really going through with this?
Nothing can stop you now?

11
00:00:33,532 --> 00:00:34,685
Don’t worry, Lola.

12
00:00:36,353 --> 00:00:40,325
Tash and I will always come back to
visit because, of course, we’ll miss you.

13
00:00:43,007 --> 00:00:44,115
Only Lola?

14
00:00:44,851 --> 00:00:45,871
Of course, you too!

15
00:00:48,076 --> 00:00:50,956
All of you! All of you, okay?

16
00:00:51,442 --> 00:00:55,276
Just make sure to take
care of yourselves there.

17
00:00:55,301 --> 00:00:57,907
Watch your stuff—someone
might steal from you.

18
00:00:58,108 --> 00:01:02,905
Take care of yourselves, and
don’t forget my souvenir, okay?

19
00:01:03,890 --> 00:01:04,903
Yes, Lola.

20
00:01:05,906 --> 00:01:08,120
Anne, do you have anything to say?

21
00:01:08,366 --> 00:01:09,440
Huh?

22
00:01:09,548 --> 00:01:11,588
Not really. I’ll just text you.

23
00:01:13,180 --> 00:01:14,252
Text me now.

24
00:01:15,007 --> 00:01:16,220
- So I can read it already.
- Right now?

25
00:01:18,708 --> 00:01:19,815
What’s with that?

26
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:21,354
Wow, you must have a lot of load!

27
00:01:22,132 --> 00:01:22,739
Fine. Now?

28
00:01:22,816 --> 00:01:24,329
Yes, now, so I can read it.

29
00:01:24,700 --> 00:01:25,386
Alright then.

30
00:01:29,654 --> 00:01:31,764
- That’s a long text!
- Wow.

31
00:01:37,796 --> 00:01:39,062
Why don’t you just say it?

32
00:01:39,571 --> 00:01:41,917
Come on, Orb! That’s barely anything!

33
00:01:43,816 --> 00:01:45,436
Wow, you texted a lot!

34
00:01:46,011 --> 00:01:46,968
Not really!

35
00:01:46,993 --> 00:01:49,306
Oh, and look at this—wow!

36
00:01:49,348 --> 00:01:51,381
You even put "no girls," huh?

37
00:01:53,542 --> 00:01:56,253
- Unbelievable!
- That’s your message, huh?

38
00:01:56,278 --> 00:01:59,730
Small?! You even outdid Lola.

39
00:02:01,231 --> 00:02:02,324
No, I didn’t!

40
00:02:02,674 --> 00:02:04,254
Just make sure you’ll miss me, okay?

41
00:02:04,912 --> 00:02:05,957
Oh, for sure!

42
00:02:07,607 --> 00:02:09,254
Wow, it’s getting hot in here!

43
00:03:12,614 --> 00:03:17,707
I was about to buy some load, but I
lost my... wait, I lost my twenty.

44
00:03:18,164 --> 00:03:19,856
Hey, did you guys see my twenty?

45
00:03:20,140 --> 00:03:21,414
Her twenty?

46
00:03:21,439 --> 00:03:22,192
Twenty?

47
00:03:22,236 --> 00:03:24,535
Wow, you own a store, and
you don’t even have twenty?

48
00:03:24,816 --> 00:03:26,439
- Did you see my twenty?
- No!

49
00:03:27,339 --> 00:03:28,474
I don’t even know.

50
00:03:28,591 --> 00:03:29,323
Then what’s this?

51
00:03:29,348 --> 00:03:30,060
Ay!

52
00:03:30,085 --> 00:03:31,545
Are you serious?!

53
00:03:33,606 --> 00:03:34,886
I thought you changed!

54
00:03:36,501 --> 00:03:37,759
Boss Beauty!

55
00:03:37,784 --> 00:03:39,184
Come on, it’s just twenty!

56
00:03:39,209 --> 00:03:40,979
What the heck, Chard?!

57
00:03:41,056 --> 00:03:43,710
It’s just twenty! You’re being so stingy!

58
00:03:43,836 --> 00:03:45,943
Here, twenty, for load.

59
00:03:45,968 --> 00:03:46,943
Ah, okay.

60
00:03:46,968 --> 00:03:48,030
Wow, look at this one.

61
00:03:48,055 --> 00:03:50,455
Hey, Mariposa, Boss Beauty!

62
00:03:50,486 --> 00:03:52,310
- Iskineport!
- Have you seen Tso K?

63
00:03:52,623 --> 00:03:53,843
- Tso K?
- Tso K?

64
00:03:54,180 --> 00:03:55,428
Not yet!

65
00:03:55,453 --> 00:03:57,001
Where could he have gone?

66
00:03:57,026 --> 00:03:57,713
Why?

67
00:03:57,738 --> 00:04:03,212
Well, I was planning to rent this vacant
store here and turn it into my tattoo shop.

68
00:04:03,237 --> 00:04:05,654
It’s my dream, and
it’s finally coming true!

69
00:04:06,179 --> 00:04:07,342
That’s why I’m looking for him.

70
00:04:07,367 --> 00:04:09,007
- Oh, I see.
- Oh, a business?

71
00:04:09,032 --> 00:04:12,639
You better study it first.

72
00:04:12,677 --> 00:04:18,062
That’s pretty tough. Maybe
you need a feasibility study.

73
00:04:18,654 --> 00:04:20,387
A what? What did you say?

74
00:04:20,554 --> 00:04:22,507
Feasibility study!

75
00:04:22,538 --> 00:04:23,398
Oh, big word!

76
00:04:23,878 --> 00:04:24,438
Yes!

77
00:04:24,463 --> 00:04:25,262
Oh, spell it?

78
00:04:25,550 --> 00:04:27,384
- Ah...
- Spell!

79
00:04:27,483 --> 00:04:30,203
Ah... uh... F...

80
00:04:30,402 --> 00:04:33,689
and... whatever, I know it has an “S”!

81
00:04:33,714 --> 00:04:36,852
You know what, just go
ahead and start your business!

82
00:04:36,877 --> 00:04:38,697
- Go, go, go!
- You have so many suggestions...

83
00:04:38,722 --> 00:04:40,603
...but you can’t even spell feasibility!

84
00:04:40,628 --> 00:04:41,274
That’s not the point,
just start it already!

85
00:04:41,306 --> 00:04:43,318
- But how do you really spell feasibility?
- Yeah?

86
00:04:47,217 --> 00:04:51,618
Oh, but where will you get...
you know, the rent money?

87
00:04:51,673 --> 00:04:53,740
Do you have a deposit?

88
00:04:53,797 --> 00:04:55,631
Do you have a cash advance?

89
00:04:55,933 --> 00:04:57,029
Do you even have money?

90
00:04:58,345 --> 00:05:03,661
No, really! That’s why I’m looking
for Tso K—I need to borrow capital.

91
00:05:03,686 --> 00:05:04,019
Ah...

92
00:05:04,057 --> 00:05:07,180
Because I also want him to
meet my partner, Che-che.

93
00:05:07,257 --> 00:05:09,010
- Who’s Che-che?
- She looks exactly like Chacha.

94
00:05:09,437 --> 00:05:10,931
- Ate Cha?
- Wooh!

95
00:05:11,155 --> 00:05:14,108
Oh, so Tso K was here all
along! And none of you told me?!

96
00:05:14,134 --> 00:05:15,136
Have you been here this whole time, Tso K?

97
00:05:15,184 --> 00:05:18,569
I’ve been here the whole time! How
could you not see me?! I was eating!

98
00:05:18,594 --> 00:05:21,982
And you, don’t go around saying that
your friend looks like my Chacha, okay?

99
00:05:22,282 --> 00:05:23,857
She really does look like Che-che!

100
00:05:24,135 --> 00:05:29,484
No way, because my Cha is the
one and only beauty queen in my life!

101
00:05:29,565 --> 00:05:31,311
No one else could ever compare!

102
00:05:31,736 --> 00:05:32,982
She really looks like her, though.

103
00:05:33,914 --> 00:05:35,361
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

104
00:05:35,563 --> 00:05:39,789
Iskineport, if that’s not
true, you’re in big trouble.

105
00:05:41,062 --> 00:05:42,037
Wait,

106
00:05:42,894 --> 00:05:45,287
what about your job with BFF

107
00:05:45,684 --> 00:05:47,998
if you’re going to do tattoos?

108
00:05:49,130 --> 00:05:51,417
No problem, Tso K.

109
00:05:51,749 --> 00:05:57,819
I can still work for Kuya Aga because
I have a partner—we’ll take turns.

110
00:05:58,103 --> 00:05:59,643
She’s really good at tattooing—

111
00:06:00,154 --> 00:06:01,394
her name’s Jen!

112
00:06:02,744 --> 00:06:04,717
Whoa, is that for real?

113
00:06:04,742 --> 00:06:07,416
- This guy keeps mentioning girls’ names...
- You have a partner?

114
00:06:07,441 --> 00:06:07,963
Yes!

115
00:06:07,988 --> 00:06:08,876
- Jen?
- Jen?

116
00:06:08,901 --> 00:06:10,064
They’re all beautiful!

117
00:06:10,089 --> 00:06:10,815
Is she a beauty, too?

118
00:06:10,840 --> 00:06:11,966
Here she is—Jen!

119
00:06:11,991 --> 00:06:13,857
- Hello!
- Jen!

120
00:06:14,048 --> 00:06:14,914
She’s here.

121
00:06:15,764 --> 00:06:16,777
Where will we do the tattoos?

122
00:06:16,817 --> 00:06:19,344
Right here! Who wants a tattoo?!

123
00:06:19,484 --> 00:06:21,037
- Me!
- Me!

124
00:06:21,062 --> 00:06:22,028
Me!

125
00:06:22,053 --> 00:06:23,107
I want a tattoo!

126
00:06:25,030 --> 00:06:26,086
We’re getting tattoos!

127
00:06:26,111 --> 00:06:27,137
Are you getting one?

128
00:06:27,162 --> 00:06:27,961
I am.

129
00:06:27,986 --> 00:06:30,083
Alright then, take off
your shirt. Take it off.

130
00:06:30,175 --> 00:06:31,568
Take off your shirt first!

131
00:06:32,215 --> 00:06:34,449
There’ll be blood splatter!

132
00:06:34,474 --> 00:06:35,866
Come on... why
won’t you take it off?!

133
00:06:36,489 --> 00:06:39,757
Do you have a rash or something?!
Where do you want your tattoo?!

134
00:06:39,782 --> 00:06:41,457
Here, here! I want it here!

135
00:06:41,482 --> 00:06:44,462
Sure! You go first!

136
00:06:45,378 --> 00:06:48,138
- Th–that’s what you’re using?!
- Yes, this!

137
00:06:48,461 --> 00:06:50,048
No escape now!

138
00:06:53,898 --> 00:06:55,311
The takoyaki ran away!

139
00:06:55,915 --> 00:06:58,392
Who else wants a tattoo?! You?!

140
00:06:59,130 --> 00:07:00,596
The takoyaki ran away—

141
00:07:00,621 --> 00:07:03,381
I thought they wanted a tattoo!

142
00:07:03,839 --> 00:07:05,266
I thought we were
tattooing—why is it like this?

143
00:07:05,291 --> 00:07:06,231
Why does it look like that?

144
00:07:06,256 --> 00:07:07,615
Is that... a coconut?!

145
00:07:08,350 --> 00:07:10,438
This is my specialty—I learned this.

146
00:07:10,463 --> 00:07:11,936
That looks terrifying!

147
00:07:12,185 --> 00:07:13,405
Is that the only thing you’re good at?

148
00:07:13,430 --> 00:07:15,620
- Yes! But there’s more!
- What?

149
00:07:15,652 --> 00:07:18,300
- Do you want to know? Do you want to know?
- I don’t want to know.

150
00:07:25,382 --> 00:07:26,437
Where is it?

151
00:07:26,462 --> 00:07:27,823
Oh, maybe it’s here?

152
00:07:29,869 --> 00:07:32,375
Where did our passports go?!

153
00:07:33,774 --> 00:07:35,341
You were the last one holding them.

154
00:07:36,559 --> 00:07:40,539
Gra—hey, are you guys pranking us?!

155
00:07:40,906 --> 00:07:41,926
This isn’t funny.

156
00:07:42,269 --> 00:07:44,129
Us?! Why us?!

157
00:07:44,786 --> 00:07:47,399
Why are you blaming us?!

158
00:07:47,910 --> 00:07:49,357
We didn’t take anything.

159
00:07:49,816 --> 00:07:50,316
You’re overreacting.

160
00:07:50,341 --> 00:07:51,548
Maybe... Anne?

161
00:07:52,588 --> 00:07:55,648
Huh? Me?! Hey, it wasn’t me!

162
00:07:56,415 --> 00:07:59,329
Well, I’d be happy if they weren’t leaving,

163
00:08:00,272 --> 00:08:04,479
but I wouldn’t go as far as
hiding their passports, okay?

164
00:08:04,911 --> 00:08:08,224
I know how important
their trip to Singapore is.

165
00:08:10,481 --> 00:08:13,314
What if we rush our passport renewal?

166
00:08:13,750 --> 00:08:14,772
Rush it?

167
00:08:14,797 --> 00:08:17,044
Tash, you know
that takes a long time.

168
00:08:17,683 --> 00:08:22,315
Even with an affidavit, we
won’t get them right away.

169
00:08:22,842 --> 00:08:24,328
It won’t be ready by tomorrow.

170
00:08:26,123 --> 00:08:28,117
Oh, have you found your passports yet?

171
00:08:28,541 --> 00:08:29,586
Not yet.

172
00:08:31,075 --> 00:08:35,961
You know, you won’t find
them if you just keep talking.

173
00:08:36,551 --> 00:08:39,285
Your mom and I will help
you look for them, okay?

174
00:08:39,316 --> 00:08:40,954
We’ll find them—they’re
just here somewhere!

175
00:08:41,045 --> 00:08:41,979
That’s the thing, Dad.

176
00:08:42,004 --> 00:08:45,076
We’ve already searched the whole
house, and they’re nowhere to be found.

177
00:08:45,101 --> 00:08:45,833
You did what?

178
00:08:45,858 --> 00:08:47,171
The whole house.

179
00:08:47,196 --> 00:08:47,768
What happened?

180
00:08:47,800 --> 00:08:51,529
We searched the whole house,
and they’re really not there.

181
00:08:51,675 --> 00:08:53,562
- Searched the—
- So, what do we do now? Huh?

182
00:08:56,399 --> 00:08:57,086
Kuya Aga!

183
00:08:57,111 --> 00:08:58,754
- Oh?
- Kuya Aga, Ate Cha!

184
00:08:58,779 --> 00:08:59,522
Iskineport.

185
00:08:59,578 --> 00:09:00,918
I want to introduce you
to someone. Come here.

186
00:09:01,144 --> 00:09:02,250
Hello!

187
00:09:02,302 --> 00:09:03,375
This is Ate Cha.

188
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:04,320
Hello!

189
00:09:04,652 --> 00:09:08,522
This is Jen—she’s my tattooing partner.

190
00:09:08,704 --> 00:09:10,194
She does tattoos too.

191
00:09:10,219 --> 00:09:11,500
Jen, this is Kuya Aga.

192
00:09:13,923 --> 00:09:17,183
Good morning!
I have something...

193
00:09:17,349 --> 00:09:18,843
- What?
- For you.

194
00:09:20,263 --> 00:09:23,889
It’s sweet, just like me.

195
00:09:25,946 --> 00:09:28,460
Hey, my love, why is it that

196
00:09:28,485 --> 00:09:31,572
every time we have a guest,
you’re always touching them...

197
00:09:31,597 --> 00:09:32,664
and even giving kisses?!

198
00:09:32,695 --> 00:09:35,607
No, they’re like my kids!

199
00:09:35,632 --> 00:09:36,378
What?!

200
00:09:36,403 --> 00:09:38,027
Why are you stuttering?
Are you having a stroke?

201
00:09:38,052 --> 00:09:38,998
What? Say that again!

202
00:09:39,023 --> 00:09:40,655
Ba-ba-ba-because there’s—

203
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:42,143
He’s making so many excuses!

204
00:09:42,168 --> 00:09:43,429
Then return it if you don’t want it!

205
00:09:43,454 --> 00:09:44,003
It's okay.

206
00:09:44,027 --> 00:09:45,860
Say that again, my love?

207
00:09:45,931 --> 00:09:47,444
Never mind. Just continue
what you were saying.

208
00:09:47,741 --> 00:09:49,062
Do you want this candy?

209
00:09:49,683 --> 00:09:50,742
Do you want it or not?

210
00:09:50,774 --> 00:09:51,923
Fine, I’ll just put it in my pocket.

211
00:09:51,948 --> 00:09:53,008
- Alright, then.
- Okay.

212
00:09:53,968 --> 00:09:57,750
Oh, here’s another
candy, give it to him again.

213
00:10:04,832 --> 00:10:08,731
Boss Beauty, Mariposa, did
you guys see the kids’ passports?

214
00:10:08,756 --> 00:10:10,022
They’re missing.

215
00:10:10,047 --> 00:10:11,930
Oh no, Ate Cha, no.

216
00:10:11,955 --> 00:10:15,755
But if we find them, don’t worry,
we’ll give them to you right away.

217
00:10:15,827 --> 00:10:16,553
Yes.

218
00:10:16,578 --> 00:10:19,503
And was it right for us to
ask them for their passports?

219
00:10:19,528 --> 00:10:20,967
- Yeah, right?!
- Hey!

220
00:10:21,087 --> 00:10:22,134
- Hi!
- Tso K!

221
00:10:22,159 --> 00:10:23,540
- BFF!
- Hey, BFF!

222
00:10:24,314 --> 00:10:26,421
Your aura seems different today.

223
00:10:26,445 --> 00:10:27,932
You look happy.

224
00:10:27,957 --> 00:10:32,513
Of course, Kuya Aga!
She saw me again! Right?

225
00:10:32,538 --> 00:10:33,526
Love you too!

226
00:10:33,551 --> 00:10:34,210
No way!

227
00:10:34,235 --> 00:10:36,251
What are you talking
about? That’s ridiculous!

228
00:10:36,791 --> 00:10:37,791
No…

229
00:10:37,816 --> 00:10:39,126
Whoa, you’re looking at me differently…

230
00:10:39,171 --> 00:10:42,779
No, I’m just really happy
because, of course, I saw my “labs”!

231
00:10:42,920 --> 00:10:44,640
Oh?! Your “labs”?!

232
00:10:45,644 --> 00:10:47,384
I thought we were good?

233
00:10:47,445 --> 00:10:49,539
Didn’t we agree to move on?

234
00:10:49,564 --> 00:10:50,414
What?

235
00:10:50,439 --> 00:10:53,127
- Move on, right?
- Relax, BFF!

236
00:10:53,238 --> 00:10:55,278
It’s not Chacha!

237
00:10:55,754 --> 00:11:01,932
I already have Cheche, Iskineport’s
business partner at the tattoo shop.

238
00:11:02,074 --> 00:11:04,478
That’s why things are kind of okay.

239
00:11:04,883 --> 00:11:06,010
- In fairness, huh?
- What?

240
00:11:06,380 --> 00:11:07,114
She looks like you.

241
00:11:07,986 --> 00:11:10,040
She looks like me?! Cheche?!

242
00:11:10,065 --> 00:11:11,315
- Yeah!
- Really?

243
00:11:11,340 --> 00:11:12,022
Yeah!

244
00:11:12,665 --> 00:11:15,685
Why don’t you show me? Show
me. What, does she even exist?

245
00:11:15,820 --> 00:11:18,807
Of course! Why would I…would I lie?

246
00:11:18,836 --> 00:11:20,736
I even thought you were twins.

247
00:11:20,873 --> 00:11:24,057
Alright, Tso K, if you
show me and she really

248
00:11:24,081 --> 00:11:27,701
looks like Ate Cha, I
promise, I will step back!

249
00:11:27,980 --> 00:11:28,600
Oh!

250
00:11:28,625 --> 00:11:29,613
- Oh!
- Let’s see!

251
00:11:29,882 --> 00:11:31,017
- Really?
- Yes!

252
00:11:31,042 --> 00:11:31,842
Alright, I’ll show you!

253
00:11:31,888 --> 00:11:33,895
Uh, okay, let’s see!

254
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:35,475
- Alright, let’s see it then!
- Let me see?

255
00:11:35,500 --> 00:11:37,422
Let’s see, come on.

256
00:11:37,487 --> 00:11:39,320
Wait, I just need to
adjust the screen. Hold on.

257
00:11:39,826 --> 00:11:40,957
I’m still fixing it.

258
00:11:40,982 --> 00:11:43,709
Don’t rush me,
it’s hard to find.

259
00:11:44,871 --> 00:11:45,858
Don’t move it!

260
00:11:46,648 --> 00:11:47,562
There!

261
00:11:47,587 --> 00:11:48,312
Swipe.

262
00:11:48,337 --> 00:11:49,513
That’s it!

263
00:11:49,538 --> 00:11:50,335
What’s that?

264
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:51,767
- Looks…
- Blurry?

265
00:11:52,857 --> 00:11:53,830
One more, one more.

266
00:11:54,865 --> 00:11:55,812
Mmm, okay, here.

267
00:11:55,837 --> 00:11:56,736
She’s facing away!

268
00:11:56,761 --> 00:11:58,100
That’s just hair!

269
00:11:59,105 --> 00:12:01,418
You guys are too much…Oh!

270
00:12:04,818 --> 00:12:08,310
In fairness, Tso K, you almost got it.

271
00:12:09,103 --> 00:12:11,421
It was so close! You were so close!

272
00:12:11,446 --> 00:12:12,308
But it’s like there was nothing there!

273
00:12:12,333 --> 00:12:13,765
We didn’t see anything!

274
00:12:13,790 --> 00:12:15,215
There wasn’t even a girl there!

275
00:12:15,870 --> 00:12:18,224
You keep looking, but
you complain so much!

276
00:12:18,249 --> 00:12:19,250
You all have so many problems!

277
00:12:19,275 --> 00:12:21,938
Whatever, I’ve got somewhere to be!

278
00:12:22,282 --> 00:12:23,909
I have a date with my “labs”!

279
00:12:25,519 --> 00:12:26,925
Whooo, we’re going on a date!

280
00:12:27,691 --> 00:12:30,145
Ha, Tso K has a love life now?

281
00:12:30,292 --> 00:12:32,719
So if you’re an alien,
you take small steps?

282
00:12:37,673 --> 00:12:38,847
- My love…
- Mmm?

283
00:12:38,872 --> 00:12:40,637
I’m sure it’s here somewhere.

284
00:12:41,080 --> 00:12:43,367
That’s what I’m saying,
they’re just messy!

285
00:12:44,130 --> 00:12:48,244
Oh, my love, like you
weren’t like that at their age!

286
00:12:48,269 --> 00:12:48,822
Mmm?

287
00:12:48,847 --> 00:12:50,860
Just be patient with them.

288
00:12:51,162 --> 00:12:53,602
We’ll find their passports soon! Right?

289
00:12:54,938 --> 00:12:55,928
Right?

290
00:12:55,953 --> 00:12:59,334
Hey, look at this, my love, a songbook!

291
00:13:00,171 --> 00:13:03,124
Do people still use
songbooks? Look at this!

292
00:13:04,006 --> 00:13:06,773
And you’re still surprised? Look at this!

293
00:13:07,087 --> 00:13:08,022
Oh…

294
00:13:08,047 --> 00:13:09,487
Wow, this is so old!

295
00:13:09,978 --> 00:13:11,526
- No, here’s what we’ll do…
- Oh?

296
00:13:11,551 --> 00:13:17,518
Let’s just do a general cleaning of the
house and look for it while we’re at it.

297
00:13:17,635 --> 00:13:19,868
That’s a good idea. Let’s do that.

298
00:13:22,676 --> 00:13:24,105
- You see?
- You see, right?

299
00:13:24,130 --> 00:13:27,179
We really prepared
that room for you.

300
00:13:27,405 --> 00:13:32,412
One bed is for you, and
then the other one is for us.

301
00:13:32,437 --> 00:13:33,286
Yeah.

302
00:13:33,311 --> 00:13:34,158
Where were you?

303
00:13:34,183 --> 00:13:35,068
Uh…uh?

304
00:13:35,100 --> 00:13:37,748
Oh, Ate Cha, Kuya Aga, you’re here.

305
00:13:37,773 --> 00:13:38,141
Yeah.

306
00:13:38,166 --> 00:13:41,118
Good thing you’re here, so
you’ll know what we’re planning.

307
00:13:41,143 --> 00:13:41,722
What?

308
00:13:41,747 --> 00:13:47,622
Since Tash and Andres aren’t here
anymore, she’ll stay in their room for now.

309
00:13:48,020 --> 00:13:48,947
She’ll sleep there.

310
00:13:48,972 --> 00:13:49,684
In the room?

311
00:13:49,709 --> 00:13:50,730
Tash and Andres’ room.

312
00:13:50,755 --> 00:13:51,927
She’s looking for a room?

313
00:13:51,952 --> 00:13:53,559
Tash and Andres already left.

314
00:13:53,893 --> 00:13:55,887
Uh…my love! My love, is that okay?!

315
00:13:55,912 --> 00:13:57,238
Are you okay with that?!

316
00:13:57,290 --> 00:13:59,250
Come on, Ate Cha, it
would be a waste of space.

317
00:13:59,275 --> 00:14:00,813
Are you really okay with that?!

318
00:14:00,838 --> 00:14:01,924
I got this.

319
00:14:02,245 --> 00:14:04,234
- So, you’re staying in that room?
- Yes.

320
00:14:05,270 --> 00:14:06,528
- Really?
- Yes.

321
00:14:06,796 --> 00:14:08,196
It would be a waste of space, Kuya Aga.

322
00:14:08,221 --> 00:14:09,994
So you’re just making decisions now?

323
00:14:10,831 --> 00:14:14,721
We own this house, and you’re
just letting someone use a room?

324
00:14:15,564 --> 00:14:16,580
Is that right?

325
00:14:17,114 --> 00:14:17,907
Sorry, Kuya Aga.

326
00:14:17,932 --> 00:14:19,604
Yeah, you really should be sorry.

327
00:14:19,629 --> 00:14:22,227
You should’ve told us. You can’t just –

328
00:14:22,354 --> 00:14:23,147
- Kuya Aga…
- Yes?

329
00:14:23,172 --> 00:14:25,938
It’s just temporary.

330
00:14:26,686 --> 00:14:29,239
Until the tattoo shop opens.

331
00:14:30,518 --> 00:14:32,005
Weren’t you guys looking for something?

332
00:14:32,030 --> 00:14:33,283
Mm-mm, the passports.

333
00:14:33,308 --> 00:14:34,055
I can help you.

334
00:14:34,080 --> 00:14:35,657
Ow, ow, that hurts! What the heck?!

335
00:14:35,682 --> 00:14:36,693
Behave!

336
00:14:36,718 --> 00:14:39,174
I am talking to her properly!

337
00:14:39,578 --> 00:14:40,831
Do you want another one?!

338
00:14:40,980 --> 00:14:42,087
Wait! My love…

339
00:14:42,112 --> 00:14:42,830
Mmm?

340
00:14:43,226 --> 00:14:43,691
What?

341
00:14:43,716 --> 00:14:44,836
I’m really good at finding things.

342
00:14:44,861 --> 00:14:46,168
Let’s find the passports.

343
00:14:46,327 --> 00:14:47,885
Come on, let’s go find them.
Let’s find—ow! Let’s find the passports!

344
00:14:48,500 --> 00:14:51,133
Let’s find—ow! Let’s
find the passports!

345
00:14:51,292 --> 00:14:52,839
Where is she staying?
Where is she sleeping?

346
00:14:52,864 --> 00:14:53,807
Here!

347
00:14:54,127 --> 00:14:55,020
With you!

348
00:14:55,045 --> 00:14:56,715
I thought you didn’t want that?!

349
00:14:56,740 --> 00:14:58,337
Well, it would be a waste of space.

350
00:14:58,362 --> 00:14:59,181
Exactly!

351
00:14:59,219 --> 00:15:00,838
- Told you!
- It’s fine, my love.

352
00:15:00,863 --> 00:15:02,469
I thought you said you got this?

353
00:15:02,759 --> 00:15:04,232
I do. Look, it’s all settled.

354
00:15:04,290 --> 00:15:05,483
Okay, you can use the room.

355
00:15:05,508 --> 00:15:06,281
Yes!

356
00:15:08,274 --> 00:15:10,234
Thank you! Yay! I’m going up now.

357
00:15:10,259 --> 00:15:11,507
- Go on up.
- Thank you!

358
00:15:15,636 --> 00:15:17,556
Kuya, I’m so scared.

359
00:15:17,847 --> 00:15:19,309
What if we can’t fly out?

360
00:15:19,643 --> 00:15:21,763
What are our bosses
going to do to us?

361
00:15:22,730 --> 00:15:23,638
Kuya?

362
00:15:26,757 --> 00:15:27,963
Kuya, are you with us?

363
00:15:27,988 --> 00:15:31,138
Huh? Sorry, sorry,
sorry, I was just thinking.

364
00:15:32,288 --> 00:15:35,628
What if fate is making
a way for us to leave?

365
00:15:37,930 --> 00:15:38,703
You know, Orb,

366
00:15:40,366 --> 00:15:42,753
I feel you, and I agree.

367
00:15:43,448 --> 00:15:45,568
But don’t you guys have a contract?

368
00:15:45,823 --> 00:15:47,776
Exactly, Kuya!

369
00:15:48,127 --> 00:15:53,451
And Kuya, we worked so hard to
build this career for a good future, right?

370
00:15:53,790 --> 00:15:56,169
And now what, we’re just
going to throw it all away?

371
00:15:56,368 --> 00:15:57,341
For what?

372
00:15:57,366 --> 00:15:58,516
I don’t even know!

373
00:15:59,412 --> 00:16:01,352
You, why did you lose the passport?!

374
00:16:01,498 --> 00:16:02,610
You were the one holding it!

375
00:16:02,635 --> 00:16:03,618
Are you blaming me?

376
00:16:04,223 --> 00:16:05,930
I just put it on the table!

377
00:16:06,694 --> 00:16:08,754
Okay, okay, enough.

378
00:16:09,304 --> 00:16:11,784
Let’s just go back inside and check again.

379
00:16:12,303 --> 00:16:15,876
Maybe we missed something.
Let’s try looking again.

380
00:16:17,583 --> 00:16:18,278
Alright.

381
00:16:18,303 --> 00:16:20,083
Yes, yes! Of course!

382
00:16:20,688 --> 00:16:21,719
I miss you, too!

383
00:16:22,387 --> 00:16:24,100
I miss you, too, my love!

384
00:16:24,926 --> 00:16:26,846
Don’t worry, tomorrow!
Tomorrow, we’ll see each other!

385
00:16:27,270 --> 00:16:29,234
We’ll see each other again, okay?

386
00:16:31,409 --> 00:16:32,722
Wow, you smell so good!

387
00:16:36,619 --> 00:16:37,649
So pretty!

388
00:16:38,032 --> 00:16:39,392
Tso K, who’s that?

389
00:16:41,027 --> 00:16:42,123
My labs!

390
00:16:42,148 --> 00:16:43,395
I’m talking to my labs!

391
00:16:44,532 --> 00:16:46,198
This is going to be
your future aunt, okay?

392
00:16:47,243 --> 00:16:49,659
Soon! Here, look!
So pretty, right?

393
00:16:51,160 --> 00:16:53,594
You’re messing with
us. There’s nothing there.

394
00:16:53,912 --> 00:16:55,820
Oh no, the call got cut off!

395
00:16:55,950 --> 00:16:57,045
No, it didn’t!

396
00:17:00,094 --> 00:17:02,253
Maybe the signal is just weak!

397
00:17:02,278 --> 00:17:05,073
You guys are really laughing at me, huh?!

398
00:17:05,098 --> 00:17:07,554
But it’s fine, I’m happy!

399
00:17:14,054 --> 00:17:16,234
Was Tso K really talking to someone?

400
00:17:16,259 --> 00:17:18,260
I don’t know, it looked
like no one was there.

401
00:17:18,504 --> 00:17:20,444
He’s been acting weird.

402
00:17:21,061 --> 00:17:23,394
Uh, hello, guys, the passports! Remember?

403
00:17:23,809 --> 00:17:26,663
Oh yeah. Maybe…

404
00:17:26,746 --> 00:17:29,006
- Tash? Let’s find them.
- Let’s find them.

405
00:17:31,558 --> 00:17:35,379
Come on, you lead the search since
you’re always zoning out! Let’s go!

406
00:17:40,718 --> 00:17:42,111
It's done.

407
00:17:42,136 --> 00:17:43,608
- Bitoy?
- Bitoy?

408
00:17:44,135 --> 00:17:45,301
Bitoy!

409
00:17:45,326 --> 00:17:47,800
Thank you! It's all good.
Don't forget the aftercare, okay?

410
00:17:47,948 --> 00:17:50,068
- Thank you! Hi, Bitoy!
- Ah, it's Bitoy!

411
00:17:52,523 --> 00:17:54,631
He greeted the cameraman!
He greeted the cameraman!

412
00:17:54,656 --> 00:17:57,555
Oh, I want one too! But not Bitoy.

413
00:17:58,513 --> 00:17:59,826
What do you want? Bitay?

414
00:17:59,856 --> 00:18:01,289
Ah… just a little heart-heart!

415
00:18:01,314 --> 00:18:02,271
Oh no, Pipay!

416
00:18:02,296 --> 00:18:05,102
Better ask your parents first, or you're
gonna get in trouble when you get home.

417
00:18:05,127 --> 00:18:06,836
You're such a buzzkill.

418
00:18:06,861 --> 00:18:08,401
Yeah, you're still kids.

419
00:18:08,452 --> 00:18:08,972
Yeah!

420
00:18:08,997 --> 00:18:11,515
You need your parents’ consent first.

421
00:18:11,540 --> 00:18:13,841
You know what, I’ll just go
ahead instead. Move aside!

422
00:18:13,872 --> 00:18:16,435
- Ouch, ouch, ouch!
- Hello! Hi, Jen!

423
00:18:16,460 --> 00:18:17,829
Hi! What design do you want?

424
00:18:17,854 --> 00:18:21,698
Tribal? That would look cool on you.

425
00:18:22,440 --> 00:18:26,053
I was just thinking of
getting my eyebrows tattooed.

426
00:18:26,078 --> 00:18:27,580
Oh, Mariposa, you're crazy.

427
00:18:27,605 --> 00:18:31,000
- Move over.
- That’s for a different shop!

428
00:18:31,030 --> 00:18:31,631
Why?

429
00:18:31,656 --> 00:18:33,404
Why would you get your
eyebrows tattooed here?!

430
00:18:33,429 --> 00:18:34,735
- Tattoo artist.
- You're nuts!

431
00:18:34,760 --> 00:18:36,448
- Me, I just want some bangs right here…
- Oh!

432
00:18:36,486 --> 00:18:38,449
Just some bangs, just
a little bit here, okay?

433
00:18:39,462 --> 00:18:40,629
Why are you so shocked?

434
00:18:40,654 --> 00:18:42,622
Are you messing with me?

435
00:18:43,923 --> 00:18:44,517
Bangs?!

436
00:18:44,542 --> 00:18:45,914
Yeah, here, look.

437
00:18:48,470 --> 00:18:50,517
You're ruining my morning.

438
00:18:50,542 --> 00:18:53,262
Okay, just give me a cross. And a church.

439
00:18:54,473 --> 00:19:00,752
I… love… you…

440
00:19:01,956 --> 00:19:02,503
Oh!

441
00:19:02,528 --> 00:19:03,900
…my love.

442
00:19:04,738 --> 00:19:05,732
My love?

443
00:19:05,757 --> 00:19:08,069
Oh! Kissing the phone now, huh?

444
00:19:08,094 --> 00:19:10,038
Tso K, you’re really
serious this time, huh?

445
00:19:10,063 --> 00:19:11,580
Of course!

446
00:19:11,732 --> 00:19:14,712
Not everyone gets a
second chance at love, right?

447
00:19:14,849 --> 00:19:22,629
And look, not only is she beautiful,
but she also looks just like her!

448
00:19:22,667 --> 00:19:25,613
And more than that, she has
everything you’d want in a woman.

449
00:19:26,433 --> 00:19:27,753
I’m so lucky. Thank you!

450
00:19:28,012 --> 00:19:30,449
But, Tso K, I think we
should be the ones to

451
00:19:30,473 --> 00:19:32,911
judge if she really
compares to Tita Cha.

452
00:19:33,448 --> 00:19:34,275
Bring her here!

453
00:19:35,197 --> 00:19:35,977
- Bring her?
- Yes!

454
00:19:36,941 --> 00:19:37,695
I can’t!

455
00:19:37,720 --> 00:19:38,548
Why?

456
00:19:38,573 --> 00:19:43,285
She’s busy! Just like me, handling
businesses, she doesn’t have time.

457
00:19:45,927 --> 00:19:55,438
And, as far as I know, there's
no Cheche in Barangay Singko.

458
00:19:55,882 --> 00:20:00,803
Tso K, are you just making
this up to make me jealous?

459
00:20:01,465 --> 00:20:03,878
Because if you are, it’s working!

460
00:20:04,715 --> 00:20:05,684
What?!

461
00:20:05,709 --> 00:20:07,029
What are you saying?

462
00:20:07,681 --> 00:20:09,894
That I’m losing my mind? That I'm crazy?

463
00:20:10,073 --> 00:20:11,426
That I’m just imagining things?

464
00:20:11,971 --> 00:20:12,794
What?!

465
00:20:12,819 --> 00:20:14,616
Come on, Mariposa,
you’re being ridiculous.

466
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:17,760
- That’s harsh.
- That’s twice now.

467
00:20:18,138 --> 00:20:20,491
You know what, that Cheche does exist.

468
00:20:20,881 --> 00:20:24,511
But… she was paid to
pretend to be his girlfriend.

469
00:20:24,536 --> 00:20:26,695
- Oh!
- See? That’s how it is.

470
00:20:26,726 --> 00:20:28,372
- Oh, really?
- Yeah, she was paid.

471
00:20:28,397 --> 00:20:31,832
You guys are really making it seem
like I’m just making this all up, huh?

472
00:20:32,434 --> 00:20:33,654
I hate being embarrassed.

473
00:20:34,046 --> 00:20:36,428
Fine, I’ll prove it to you. Jen!

474
00:20:36,585 --> 00:20:37,905
- Yes, Tso K?
- I’m getting one!

475
00:20:40,043 --> 00:20:41,191
Go ahead, Jen!

476
00:20:41,338 --> 00:20:42,824
Give me a tattoo!

477
00:20:43,255 --> 00:20:44,581
Put "Cheche"!

478
00:20:44,739 --> 00:20:45,925
Make it big!

479
00:20:47,316 --> 00:20:49,222
I really hate being embarrassed!

480
00:20:49,622 --> 00:20:50,982
Are you sure?

481
00:20:51,142 --> 00:20:52,129
Of course!

482
00:20:52,154 --> 00:20:53,191
Are you sure?

483
00:20:54,567 --> 00:20:56,628
Hurry up. I don’t want this to take long.

484
00:20:57,730 --> 00:20:59,090
Oh, that doesn’t hurt?

485
00:20:59,115 --> 00:21:00,574
- Wow, so brave!
- For love!

486
00:21:06,355 --> 00:21:10,895
Lola, we’ve already thrown that
away, and you keep taking it back?

487
00:21:11,313 --> 00:21:14,599
Because it has sentimental value!

488
00:21:14,667 --> 00:21:19,473
Roman and I bought this back in
the day! When he was still alive!

489
00:21:20,079 --> 00:21:23,612
Lola, I get it.

490
00:21:23,980 --> 00:21:26,964
I mean, of course, things
that have sentimental value are

491
00:21:26,989 --> 00:21:30,207
important to you, but sometimes,
we have to move on too.

492
00:21:30,232 --> 00:21:31,332
Mmm, true!

493
00:21:31,357 --> 00:21:33,873
Right? If it’s not being
used anymore, throw it out!

494
00:21:34,241 --> 00:21:39,131
If it’s broken, it's
broken—throw it away!

495
00:21:39,586 --> 00:21:43,083
- Ugh, whatever.
- Here, look at this. Look, my love!

496
00:21:43,108 --> 00:21:43,470
Oh?

497
00:21:43,495 --> 00:21:47,595
I’m sure of it, this one, this
box! So much stuff in here–

498
00:21:47,957 --> 00:21:52,354
Oh, wait. No, this is clean! I
already cleaned it, don’t touch it.

499
00:21:52,379 --> 00:21:54,414
Go through the other stuff instead.

500
00:21:54,439 --> 00:21:55,634
Why don’t you want us to clean that?

501
00:21:55,659 --> 00:21:58,968
That’s the whole point, we’re supposed
to go through things and clean them up.

502
00:21:59,226 --> 00:22:03,120
Wait a second, what’s our goal here again?

503
00:22:03,332 --> 00:22:05,945
Aren’t we supposed to be
looking for the passports?

504
00:22:05,970 --> 00:22:06,308
Mm-hmm!

505
00:22:06,333 --> 00:22:10,861
Then why are all of you just cleaning
and throwing random stuff away?

506
00:22:11,079 --> 00:22:14,412
Let’s focus on finding
the passports first!

507
00:22:14,437 --> 00:22:16,516
Are you hiding something in there?

508
00:22:16,541 --> 00:22:18,862
- Is that why you don’t want us to open it?
- No!

509
00:22:18,946 --> 00:22:19,866
- Then there you go!
- See?

510
00:22:19,891 --> 00:22:22,325
I already cleaned it!
Why go through it again?

511
00:22:23,805 --> 00:22:25,145
What do you think, my love?

512
00:22:26,825 --> 00:22:29,819
Ah, you’re right, Lola Maxi.

513
00:22:29,844 --> 00:22:32,720
Let’s just go back to looking
for the kids’ passports.

514
00:22:32,880 --> 00:22:33,333
Mmm!

515
00:22:33,374 --> 00:22:37,014
We should check their room instead!

516
00:22:37,039 --> 00:22:37,468
There!

517
00:22:37,493 --> 00:22:39,671
Maybe their passports are
still there! Right, my love?

518
00:22:39,758 --> 00:22:42,751
- That’s the best thing to do!
- Okay! Lola Maxi…

519
00:22:42,881 --> 00:22:44,255
We’ll look over there!

520
00:22:44,280 --> 00:22:45,374
You go first!

521
00:22:45,399 --> 00:22:47,334
Yeah, let’s not just keep going in circles…

522
00:22:47,359 --> 00:22:48,782
Yeah, Lola Maxi, that’s right!

523
00:22:48,827 --> 00:22:51,310
Unlike this, where
we’re just running around

524
00:22:51,334 --> 00:22:53,817
in circles when that’s
already been cleaned!

525
00:23:03,302 --> 00:23:04,300
Open it up.

526
00:23:04,727 --> 00:23:05,722
She doesn’t want it opened.

527
00:23:05,747 --> 00:23:06,839
Yeah, she won’t let us.

528
00:23:06,864 --> 00:23:07,894
I wonder what’s inside?

529
00:23:17,373 --> 00:23:18,980
I'm really sorry, Kuya.

530
00:23:20,222 --> 00:23:23,422
I know it's my fault
that I lost our passports.

531
00:23:23,447 --> 00:23:24,249
I'm really sorry.

532
00:23:25,018 --> 00:23:26,325
Tash, it’s okay.

533
00:23:26,735 --> 00:23:28,415
We all know no one wanted this to happen.

534
00:23:29,471 --> 00:23:31,391
So… you’re not leaving anymore?

535
00:23:32,309 --> 00:23:33,369
Not anymore, Lola.

536
00:23:33,583 --> 00:23:39,617
But for now, we need to sort things out
because we have to renew our passports.

537
00:23:41,223 --> 00:23:44,270
But what if there's
already a job waiting for us?

538
00:23:45,164 --> 00:23:49,131
Oh, my dear, don’t worry!

539
00:23:49,452 --> 00:23:52,425
We’re here for you.

540
00:23:52,450 --> 00:23:59,156
We’re family, and family
sticks together, always!

541
00:23:59,943 --> 00:24:00,943
Don’t worry.

542
00:24:01,527 --> 00:24:03,020
Burn it!

543
00:24:03,558 --> 00:24:04,871
Burn it!

544
00:24:05,343 --> 00:24:06,897
Burn it!

545
00:24:07,450 --> 00:24:08,916
Burn it!

546
00:24:09,439 --> 00:24:10,855
Burn it!

547
00:24:11,857 --> 00:24:13,244
What’s happening outside?

548
00:24:13,945 --> 00:24:15,898
We should check it out!

549
00:24:16,040 --> 00:24:17,320
- Burn it!
- Come, come!

550
00:24:17,824 --> 00:24:19,191
Burn it!

551
00:24:19,650 --> 00:24:21,024
Burn it!

552
00:24:21,049 --> 00:24:22,552
Hey, wait! Wait! Wait!

553
00:24:22,577 --> 00:24:24,040
What’s that?!

554
00:24:24,157 --> 00:24:25,803
Hey! Don’t do that!

555
00:24:26,108 --> 00:24:26,875
Why not, Lola?

556
00:24:26,986 --> 00:24:28,699
Just let them! Let’s burn it!

557
00:24:28,724 --> 00:24:29,610
Burn it!

558
00:24:29,635 --> 00:24:32,343
No, no, no! You can’t do that!

559
00:24:32,368 --> 00:24:34,442
You can’t! I said stop!

560
00:24:34,663 --> 00:24:37,516
Lola, don’t interfere. That’s just trash!

561
00:24:37,541 --> 00:24:38,447
Yeah, yeah!

562
00:24:38,472 --> 00:24:41,795
No, you can’t do that
because it’s important to me!

563
00:24:42,323 --> 00:24:45,150
And what exactly is in
there? Look, it’s just junk!

564
00:24:45,553 --> 00:24:50,623
I’m telling you, it’s not trash!
It’s important to me! Don’t burn it!

565
00:24:50,912 --> 00:24:51,931
Burn it!

566
00:24:51,956 --> 00:24:53,576
Why is it so important?

567
00:24:56,653 --> 00:24:57,725
Is it because of this?

568
00:24:57,750 --> 00:24:58,503
Dad!

569
00:24:58,528 --> 00:25:00,363
- Hey!
- That’s our passports!

570
00:25:00,580 --> 00:25:02,457
- See! Look!
- Where did you find that?!

571
00:25:03,541 --> 00:25:07,561
Maybe we should ask Lola Maxi.

572
00:25:08,353 --> 00:25:12,065
- Lola Maxi…
- Well… well… my dear grandchildren…

573
00:25:12,208 --> 00:25:13,181
Come here, come here.

574
00:25:13,206 --> 00:25:14,174
I’m really sorry.

575
00:25:14,199 --> 00:25:16,816
Your Lola made a mistake.

576
00:25:17,562 --> 00:25:24,236
I hid your passports on purpose…
so you wouldn’t be able to leave.

577
00:25:25,025 --> 00:25:27,610
I just don’t understand…
why can’t we all just stay together here?

578
00:25:27,642 --> 00:25:30,227
Why do we have to be apart?

579
00:25:33,688 --> 00:25:36,248
Lola, our careers would go to waste.

580
00:25:36,889 --> 00:25:40,543
Plus, Andres and I have a
contract we need to fulfill.

581
00:25:41,628 --> 00:25:42,710
And, Lola,

582
00:25:43,650 --> 00:25:45,204
as much as we want to stay,

583
00:25:45,773 --> 00:25:48,702
we also have to build our own
careers and our own futures.

584
00:25:50,069 --> 00:25:54,043
But don’t worry, Singapore is really
close! It’s only a three-hour flight.

585
00:25:55,165 --> 00:25:56,958
We’ll visit every two weeks!

586
00:25:57,507 --> 00:25:58,947
- Wow!
- That’s a promise!

587
00:25:59,270 --> 00:26:02,243
Promise, huh? You better! I’ll be waiting!

588
00:26:02,556 --> 00:26:03,750
Every two weeks, Orb?!

589
00:26:04,133 --> 00:26:05,144
Yes!

590
00:26:05,558 --> 00:26:07,398
Look how happy someone is over there!

591
00:26:11,505 --> 00:26:13,378
Don’t burn it!

592
00:26:13,524 --> 00:26:15,497
Don’t burn it!

593
00:26:15,557 --> 00:26:17,357
Don’t burn it!

594
00:26:17,382 --> 00:26:19,267
Don’t burn it!

595
00:26:19,292 --> 00:26:20,971
Don’t burn it!

596
00:26:21,082 --> 00:26:22,462
Don’t burn it!

597
00:26:24,072 --> 00:26:25,806
Guys, this is it!

598
00:26:27,359 --> 00:26:28,265
Thank you, guys.

599
00:26:28,652 --> 00:26:30,218
Thank you for everything.

600
00:26:30,979 --> 00:26:34,152
Thanks for the guidance,
the learnings, and the help.

601
00:26:35,075 --> 00:26:38,249
My dear grandchildren,
I love you all so much.

602
00:26:38,564 --> 00:26:40,644
But remember what I told you, okay?

603
00:26:41,730 --> 00:26:43,356
Yes, Lola.

604
00:26:43,960 --> 00:26:47,421
Speaking of reminders—Orb, I
have one more thing to tell you.

605
00:26:48,736 --> 00:26:50,843
Oh no, there you go
again with your reminders.

606
00:26:51,085 --> 00:26:51,612
Yeah.

607
00:26:51,637 --> 00:26:52,896
- Yeah.
- Sis.

608
00:26:57,025 --> 00:26:59,752
Anyway, good luck over there, guys!

609
00:26:59,777 --> 00:27:01,729
- Take care.
- Take care.

610
00:27:03,348 --> 00:27:04,481
Oh, and by the way,

611
00:27:04,921 --> 00:27:08,086
you’re so lucky—when you leave,
you each have your own show.

612
00:27:10,391 --> 00:27:13,284
And don’t forget, I’m a size 11, okay?

613
00:27:13,329 --> 00:27:15,309
I’m a size 4!

614
00:27:15,677 --> 00:27:17,857
Don’t believe her! She’s only a size 3!

615
00:27:17,882 --> 00:27:19,212
Wow, really?

616
00:27:20,100 --> 00:27:22,367
Your feet are so tiny,
you can barely stand!

617
00:27:25,531 --> 00:27:27,578
- Bye, Andres! Bye, Tash!
- Thank you, guys.

618
00:27:27,603 --> 00:27:32,446
Andres, Atasha, just remember
to always take care of yourselves.

619
00:27:32,831 --> 00:27:35,438
You know I’ve already
told you everything.

620
00:27:36,031 --> 00:27:37,805
Take care of yourselves, okay?

621
00:27:37,830 --> 00:27:38,911
Yes, Dad.

622
00:27:39,232 --> 00:27:42,759
And don’t forget everything
you’ve learned here.

623
00:27:43,556 --> 00:27:44,510
Of course.

624
00:27:45,738 --> 00:27:47,198
It’s simple, right?

625
00:27:47,510 --> 00:27:55,117
In good times and bad, Pers
comes first! Pers is the star!

626
00:28:00,189 --> 00:28:01,782
Group hug!

627
00:28:04,003 --> 00:28:05,187
Group hug!

628
00:28:05,212 --> 00:28:06,760
Hey, Atasha, be careful over there, okay?

629
00:28:06,785 --> 00:28:08,251
Of course!

630
00:28:09,901 --> 00:28:13,369
Andres, go over there! Over
there! Don’t come here! Go!

631
00:28:15,919 --> 00:28:16,936
Karl!

632
00:28:17,713 --> 00:28:18,920
- BFF!
- Karl!

633
00:28:19,100 --> 00:28:20,264
Karl!

634
00:28:20,621 --> 00:28:21,655
BFF!

635
00:28:22,398 --> 00:28:23,270
Oh?

636
00:28:23,295 --> 00:28:24,815
Wait, wait, wait!
They’re about to leave!

637
00:28:26,672 --> 00:28:28,364
- There it is!
- There!

638
00:28:28,389 --> 00:28:29,514
What’s going on?

639
00:28:30,282 --> 00:28:31,595
Sorry, sorry, sorry!

640
00:28:31,620 --> 00:28:34,385
What’s wrong with you? The kids were
looking for you because they already left.

641
00:28:34,410 --> 00:28:35,527
They wanted to say goodbye.

642
00:28:35,552 --> 00:28:36,823
Oh, yeah, that’s right.

643
00:28:36,848 --> 00:28:39,815
Sorry! I got a little busy.

644
00:28:40,932 --> 00:28:42,352
Cheche was here.

645
00:28:42,753 --> 00:28:47,113
Huh? Then why didn’t you
introduce Cheche to us?

646
00:28:47,859 --> 00:28:49,612
Yeah, why didn’t you
introduce Cheche to us, and—

647
00:28:51,600 --> 00:28:52,487
- Oh, why?
- What?

648
00:28:52,658 --> 00:28:53,411
What is that?!

649
00:28:54,124 --> 00:28:55,813
- This?
- What is that?!

650
00:28:56,172 --> 00:28:57,013
Che-che.

651
00:28:57,038 --> 00:28:58,752
Why do you look like that?

652
00:28:58,777 --> 00:28:59,424
Uh…

653
00:28:59,449 --> 00:29:00,822
Why does that tattoo look upside down?

654
00:29:00,861 --> 00:29:03,392
It’s not upside down! I just used to be a
little awkward with my hands. Just kidding—

655
00:29:03,765 --> 00:29:05,085
It’s upside down!

656
00:29:05,110 --> 00:29:06,360
No, it’s not!

657
00:29:06,385 --> 00:29:10,037
It’s right because when I
show it off, I pose like this!

658
00:29:10,062 --> 00:29:11,184
Oh, so that’s how it works!

659
00:29:11,209 --> 00:29:16,182
And I wanted it styled that way because
I always want Cheche close to my skin.

660
00:29:16,207 --> 00:29:18,277
- Oh, how sweet!
- Cheche is different to me.

661
00:29:18,302 --> 00:29:20,092
- So where is this Cheche?
- Yeah, where?

662
00:29:20,152 --> 00:29:21,032
Inside.

663
00:29:21,057 --> 00:29:21,945
- She’s inside?!
- Inside?!

664
00:29:22,438 --> 00:29:24,131
- Like I said—
- Tawagin mo na nga!

665
00:29:24,975 --> 00:29:27,068
I feel shy… really?

666
00:29:27,093 --> 00:29:29,740
- Yeah, hurry up!
- You really want to see Cheche?

667
00:29:29,765 --> 00:29:32,155
- Of course!
- Of course!

668
00:29:32,180 --> 00:29:34,943
- Alright, I’ll call her now.
- Go, call her! Hurry!

669
00:29:35,341 --> 00:29:36,356
Che! Che!

670
00:29:44,578 --> 00:29:47,186
Che, come here. Che, come.

671
00:29:56,332 --> 00:29:57,442
Hi!

672
00:30:09,238 --> 00:30:11,292
Surprised? What did I tell you?

673
00:30:12,519 --> 00:30:13,755
- She looks just like you!
- Che-che?

674
00:30:19,184 --> 00:30:20,247
Here she is.

675
00:30:23,674 --> 00:30:24,971
How did that happen?

676
00:30:24,996 --> 00:30:26,583
Where did you—where—wha…?

677
00:30:36,102 --> 00:30:37,169
Dad is strict.

678
00:30:37,632 --> 00:30:38,864
He has a big heart,

679
00:30:40,566 --> 00:30:43,146
but when he has a problem,
he doesn’t like asking us for help!

680
00:30:43,306 --> 00:30:44,435
He feels embarrassed!

681
00:30:48,449 --> 00:30:49,958
Aga and I are best friends.

682
00:30:51,099 --> 00:30:53,779
Why would I hold a grudge
against my best friend?

683
00:30:53,804 --> 00:30:54,938
That was a long time ago!

684
00:30:55,084 --> 00:30:56,591
Past is past!

685
00:30:57,148 --> 00:30:58,842
He’s very romantic!

686
00:31:00,114 --> 00:31:01,967
You want to talk about my husband?

687
00:31:03,564 --> 00:31:07,517
When he gets mad, he just stares like this—

688
00:31:11,107 --> 00:31:13,553
And cut! I love that!
